### Example 2: Create Snapshot and Restore

#### Create Snapshot of Volume

```bash
aws ec2 create-snapshot \
  --volume-id vol-0123456789abcdef0 \
  --description "Daily backup - WebServer data volume" \
  --tag-specifications 'ResourceType=snapshot,Tags=[{Key=Name,Value=WebServer-Backup-2025-11-25},{Key=RetentionDays,Value=30}]'
```

**Output:**
```
{
  "SnapshotId": "snap-0abcdef1234567890",
  "VolumeId": "vol-0123456789abcdef0",
  "State": "pending",
  "StartTime": "2025-11-25T16:35:00Z",
  "Description": "Daily backup - WebServer data volume"
}
```

#### Monitor Snapshot Progress

```bash
# Check snapshot status
aws ec2 describe-snapshots --snapshot-ids snap-0abcdef1234567890

# Watch progress (polling)
watch 'aws ec2 describe-snapshots --snapshot-ids snap-0abcdef1234567890 \
  --query "Snapshots[0].[Progress,State]" --output text'

# Output:
# 100% completed
```

#### Restore Volume from Snapshot

```bash
# Create new volume from snapshot in same AZ
aws ec2 create-volume \
  --snapshot-id snap-0abcdef1234567890 \
  --availability-zone us-east-1a \
  --volume-type gp3 \
  --encrypted \
  --tag-specifications 'ResourceType=volume,Tags=[{Key=Name,Value=WebServer-DataDisk-Restored}]'
```

**Output:**
```
{
  "VolumeId": "vol-0bcdef1234567890a",
  "State": "creating",
  "SnapshotId": "snap-0abcdef1234567890",
  "Size": 20,
  "VolumeType": "gp3"
}
```

#### Copy Snapshot to Another Region (Disaster Recovery)

```bash
# Copy snapshot to us-west-2 region
aws ec2 copy-snapshot \
  --source-region us-east-1 \
  --source-snapshot-id snap-0abcdef1234567890 \
  --destination-region us-west-2 \
  --description "DR copy - WebServer backup"

# Output:
# {
#   "SnapshotId": "snap-1cdef1234567890ab"
# }

# Now you can create a volume in us-west-2 from this snapshot
```

