### Example 4: Monitor Volume Performance

#### Check Volume Metrics

```bash
# Get volume metrics from CloudWatch
aws cloudwatch get-metric-statistics \
  --namespace AWS/EBS \
  --metric-name VolumeReadBytes \
  --dimensions Name=VolumeId,Value=vol-0123456789abcdef0 \
  --statistics Sum \
  --start-time 2025-11-25T00:00:00Z \
  --end-time 2025-11-25T23:59:59Z \
  --period 3600
```

#### Monitor from Linux Instance

```bash
# Install iostat utility
sudo yum install sysstat -y  # Amazon Linux
# or
sudo apt-get install sysstat -y  # Ubuntu

# Monitor I/O performance in real-time
iostat -x 1 10
# Shows: read/write throughput, IOPS, wait times

# Monitor with iotop (process-level I/O)
sudo iotop -o
```

