## Real-World Use Cases

### Use Case 1: MySQL Database Server

**Requirements:**
- High IOPS for transaction processing
- Data persistence and durability
- Encryption for compliance

**Implementation:**
```bash
# Create high-performance volume for database
aws ec2 create-volume \
  --size 500 \
  --volume-type io2 \
  --iops 20000 \
  --availability-zone us-east-1a \
  --encrypted \
  --kms-key-id alias/aws/ebs \
  --tag-specifications 'ResourceType=volume,Tags=[{Key=Name,Value=MySQL-DataVolume}]'

# Attach to database instance
aws ec2 attach-volume \
  --volume-id vol-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxx \
  --instance-id i-yyyyyyyyyyyyyyyy \
  --device /dev/xvdb

# Mount and format on instance
sudo mkfs -t ext4 /dev/xvdb
sudo mkdir /var/lib/mysql
sudo mount /dev/xvdb /var/lib/mysql
sudo chown mysql:mysql /var/lib/mysql

# Add to MySQL configuration
sudo nano /etc/my.cnf
# Add: datadir=/var/lib/mysql
```

**Benefits:**
- 20,000 IOPS for high-frequency transactions
- Encryption for compliance (PCI-DSS, HIPAA)
- Snapshots for backup and recovery

### Use Case 2: Big Data Analytics

**Requirements:**
- High throughput for sequential reads
- Cost-effective storage
- Large capacity

**Implementation:**
```bash
# Create throughput-optimized volume
aws ec2 create-volume \
  --size 2000 \
  --volume-type st1 \
  --availability-zone us-east-1a \
  --tag-specifications 'ResourceType=volume,Tags=[{Key=Name,Value=Analytics-DataVolume}]'

# Attach to analytics instance
aws ec2 attach-volume \
  --volume-id vol-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxx \
  --instance-id i-yyyyyyyyyyyyyyyy \
  --device /dev/xvdb

# Mount and format
sudo mkfs -t ext4 /dev/xvdb
sudo mkdir /data
sudo mount /dev/xvdb /data
```

**Benefits:**
- 2TB capacity at low cost
- 500 MB/s burst throughput ideal for batch processing
- Cost ~60% less than GP3 for sequential workloads

### Use Case 3: Disaster Recovery

**Requirements:**
- Regular backups
- Quick recovery
- Cross-region copies

**Implementation:**
```bash
# Create daily snapshot schedule
aws dlm create-lifecycle-policy \
  --execution-role-arn arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/service-role/AWSDataLifecycleManagerDefaultRole \
  --description "Daily snapshots for DR" \
  --state ENABLED \
  --policy-details '{
    "ResourceTypes": ["VOLUME"],
    "TargetTags": [{"Key": "Backup", "Value": "Daily"}],
    "Schedules": [{
      "Name": "DailySnapshots",
      "CopyTags": true,
      "CreateRule": {"Interval": 24, "IntervalUnit": "HOURS", "Times": ["03:00"]},
      "RetainRule": {"Count": 30},
      "CrossRegionCopyRules": [{
        "TargetRegion": "us-west-2",
        "Encrypted": true,
        "CmkArn": "arn:aws:kms:us-west-2:123456789012:key/12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012",
        "CopyTags": true,
        "RetainRule": {"Count": 30}
      }]
    }]
  }'
```

**Benefits:**
- Automated daily backups at 3 AM
- 30-day retention for point-in-time recovery
- Cross-region copies in us-west-2 for DR

